<section id="superadminGuideContent" class="role-guide d-none" data-role-guide="superadmin" data-guide-description="Account management, passwords and the shared calendar." hidden aria-label="Superadmin instructions">
<p class="role-guide-context">These controls are on the Accounts page.</p>
<h2 class="role-guide-heading" tabindex="-1">Where to click</h2>
<table class="role-guide-map" aria-label="Superadmin button locations"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Task</th><th scope="col">Find the control here</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Create an account</th><td><div class="guide-path"><strong class="guide-control"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>Create account</strong></div><small class="guide-location">Top right of the Accounts directory. Called Add account on a phone.</small></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Edit or delete an account</th><td><div class="guide-path"><strong class="guide-control"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m16 3 5 5M4 20l4-1L21 6a2 2 0 0 0-5-3L3 16l-1 5Z"/></svg>Edit</strong> or <strong class="guide-control"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6h18M9 6V3h6v3M5 6l1 15h12l1-15M10 10v7M14 10v7"/></svg>Trash icon</strong></div><small class="guide-location">Right end of that person’s row, in the Manage column.</small></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">View passwords</th><td><div class="guide-path"><strong class="guide-control"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="10" width="14" height="11" rx="2"/><path d="M8 10V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3"/></svg>View all passwords</strong></div><small class="guide-location">Above the Accounts directory. Enter your own Superadmin password.</small></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Give Staff permissions</th><td><div class="guide-path"><strong class="guide-control"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3 3 7v5c0 5 9 9 9 9s9-4 9-9V7Z"/><path d="m8 12 3 3 5-6"/></svg>Shield icon</strong> beside Edit</div><small class="guide-location">Right end of a Staff account row. Hover text: Manage permissions.</small></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Change working days</th><td><div class="guide-path"><strong>Philippine holidays</strong> → <strong class="guide-control">Manage calendar</strong></div><small class="guide-location">Below the Accounts directory. Expand it to see calendar controls.</small></td></tr></tbody></table>
<p class="role-guide-profile"><strong>Your profile:</strong> top-right avatar → <strong>Edit profile</strong> or <strong>Sign out</strong>.</p><p class="role-guide-phone">On a phone, the navigation menu is at the top.</p>
<div class="role-guide-more"><h3>Extra help, if you need it</h3><details class="role-guide-detail"><summary>Create, edit, delete and set permissions</summary><div class="role-guide-detail-body"><p><strong>Create:</strong> top-right Create account → fill name, unique username, password and role → Save account. On a phone the button says Add account. Passwords require at least 12 characters. Usernames use 3–80 letters, numbers, dots, underscores or hyphens.</p><p><strong>Edit:</strong> the Edit button at the right of the person’s row. Leave password blank to keep it. Active account controls sign-in access. Existing pending accounts offer Approve/Reject.</p><p><strong>Delete:</strong> the trash icon at the right end of an eligible row. Read the confirmation. The original Superadmin and your signed-in account cannot be deleted; keep at least one active Superadmin. Deactivate an account in Edit to stop access without removing it.</p><p><strong>Permissions:</strong> the shield icon beside Edit on Staff rows. Changes save immediately; Staff controls update automatically, usually within 15 seconds, while keeping their project drafts. Staff requests project deletion; Admin reviews and confirms it. Superadmin manages accounts and the calendar.</p></div></details><details class="role-guide-detail"><summary>View one password or reset it</summary><div class="role-guide-detail-body"><p><strong>All passwords:</strong> View all passwords is above the directory. Enter your own Superadmin password every time. Available passwords hide after 30 seconds, on close or when leaving the tab. Access is recorded. Five wrong verification attempts block viewing for five minutes.</p><p><strong>One password:</strong> find the account’s Password column → View password → enter your own Superadmin password.</p><p><strong>Available after sign-in:</strong> older passwords cannot be recovered from a hash. After that user signs in successfully once, refresh Accounts. Their password stays the same.</p><p><strong>Reset:</strong> Password column → Manage password → Set new password → enter and confirm → Save new password. This changes the person’s sign-in password. A password change signs that account out of existing sessions and clears its editing indicators. The person must sign in again; changing your own password also requires a fresh sign-in.</p></div></details><details class="role-guide-detail"><summary>Calendar, profile and signing out</summary><div class="role-guide-detail-body"><p><strong>Calendar:</strong> below Accounts → Philippine holidays → Manage calendar. Choose non-working weekdays and holiday exclusions, then save. Keep at least one working weekday. Add a named correction or restore a date to its source. Changes affect everyone’s working dates.</p><p>Enable Automatic updates and save. Sync now checks immediately; Refresh calendar reloads saved data. Review the last successful sync and coverage. Scheduled checks start at 03:00 Philippine time and need the server scheduler. A failed update keeps the last saved calendar.</p><p><strong>Your profile:</strong> top-right avatar → Edit profile. Use JPG, PNG or WebP up to 3 MB. Choose Sign out from the same menu when finished. Superadmin has no 30-minute inactivity timeout, but the eight-hour session limit still applies.</p></div></details></div>
</section>
